# Migration checksums are computed over RAW FILE BYTES (see
# backend/app/migrations.py: discover_migrations -> hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes())),
# and those checksums are persisted in schema_migrations and compared on every
# subsequent run. Line endings must therefore be byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true smudges LF -> CRLF on Windows checkout, so a
# database migrated on Windows records different checksums than the same commit
# checked out on Linux/CI/containers. The next run from the other platform sees
# checksum drift on every applied migration and refuses to apply anything.
*.sql text eol=lf
